      <h1 class="page-heading"><em>Hi,</em> I'm Pumpkin.</h1>

      <div class="about-bio">
        <p>
          My name is <strong>Bao Ngoc</strong>, but everyone calls me Pumpkin — a nickname that has somehow followed me from a quiet street in Vietnam to airports, hostels, and night markets all over the world. By day I work in social media marketing, which is a fancy way of saying I tell stories online. By every other moment I get, I'm planning the next trip, looking up flights I shouldn't book, and writing in tiny notebooks that no one will ever read.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm Vietnamese, which means I grew up understanding that food is a love language and that a good street stall beats a fancy restaurant most days of the week. Travel, for me, started as curiosity about how other people eat, gather, mourn, celebrate. Why a tea ceremony takes twenty minutes here and two hours there. Why some cities feel loud at night and others feel like a held breath.
        </p>
        <p>
          This blog is where I try to write all that down. Honestly. Slowly. With too many photos and the occasional recipe. I hope you find something useful here — and if you want to swap stories or trip recommendations, the contact form is always open.
        </p>
      </div>

